      story: "WhatsApp has more than two billion users, and in markets such as India, Brazil, and Indonesia it is where customers expect order updates, payment reminders, and support. Meta's **WhatsApp Business Platform** lets businesses send and receive messages programmatically. The self-hosted On-Premises API was retired (its final client expired on 23 October 2025), leaving the Meta-hosted **Cloud API**, which Meta describes as supporting up to 1,000 messages per second. On 1 July 2025 Meta also moved from conversation-based to **per-message pricing**, which changes how teams design notifications.",
      analogy: "Moving from running your own post office sorting machine to renting space in the national postal network, with a price list per letter type.",
      timeline: [['2018', 'WhatsApp Business API', 'Self-hosted API for large businesses.'], ['2022', 'Cloud API', 'Meta-hosted API opened broadly.'], ['1 July 2025', 'Per-message pricing', 'Charges per template message by category and country.'], ['23 October 2025', 'On-Premises API sunset', 'Final On-Premises client expired; Cloud API only.']],
      explain: "Structure: a **business portfolio** (formerly Business Manager) owns one or more **WhatsApp Business Accounts (WABAs)**, each with registered **phone numbers**. Integrate directly with the Cloud API (Graph API endpoints such as `POST /{phone-number-id}/messages`) or through a Business Solution Provider (BSP). Message kinds: **template messages** (pre-approved, needed to start conversations; categories **marketing**, **utility**, **authentication**) and **non-template (free-form) messages**, allowed only inside an open **customer service window**. **Pricing since 1 July 2025**: charges per delivered template message, by **category** and recipient **country**; service (non-template) messages inside an open window are free; **utility templates sent inside an open customer service window are free**; volume tiers can lower utility and authentication rates; entry-point windows (for example from ads that click to WhatsApp) make messages free for 72 hours. Design notifications around these rules: reply to customers within the window, keep utility messages genuinely transactional, and treat marketing as the paid channel it is.",
      diagram: "business portfolio → WABA → phone number(s) → Cloud API\ntemplate message (marketing / utility / authentication) → charged per message (by category, country)\n  utility inside open window → free\nfree-form message → only inside the 24-hour window → free\nservice window opens when the customer messages you",
      ex1: ['text', 'sending a template (Cloud API, illustrative)', "POST https://graph.facebook.com/{version}/{phone-number-id}/messages\nAuthorization: Bearer <system-user-token>\n{ \"messaging_product\": \"whatsapp\", \"to\": \"919876543210\", \"type\": \"template\",\n  \"template\": { \"name\": \"order_shipped\", \"language\": { \"code\": \"en\" },\n                \"components\": [{ \"type\": \"body\", \"parameters\": [{ \"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"Asha\" }, { \"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"#8812\" }] }] } }"],
      ex2: ['text', 'cost by situation (since 1 July 2025)', "customer messaged 2 hours ago → reply free-form: free\nsame window → utility template (order update): free\nno open window → utility template: charged\nmarketing template: charged (country rate)"],
